dy-text-mining&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;1.4k &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;804&lt;br&gt;Manuscript of the book &amp;quot;Tidy Text Mining with R&amp;quot; by Julia Silge and David Robinson&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/juliasilge/tidylo&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;tidylo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;98 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;4&lt;br&gt;Weighted tidy log odds ratio ⚖️&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/juliasilge/widyr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;widyr&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;333 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;28&lt;br&gt;Widen, process, and re-tidy a dataset&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/juliasilge/janeaustenr&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;janeaustenr&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;96 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;19&lt;br&gt;An R Package for Jane Austen&amp;#39;s Complete Novels &lt;span&gt;📙&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/juliasilge/juliasilge.com&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;juliasilge.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/star.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;star&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;44 &lt;img src=&quot;https://mshibanami.github.io/GitHubTrendingRSS/assets/icons/git-fork.png&quot; width=&quot;20&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; alt=&quot;git-fork&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0 4px 0 0; padding: 0; display: inline-block; vertical-align: middle;&quot; /&gt;25&lt;br&gt;My blog, built with blogdown and Hugo &lt;span&gt;🔗&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Hello! It&#39;s nice to meet you 👋&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I am a data scientist and engineering manager at &lt;a href=&quot;https://posit.co/&quot;&gt;Posit PBC&lt;/a&gt; where I work on tools for data science like &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/posit-dev/positron&quot;&gt;Positron&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://vetiver.posit.co/&quot;&gt;vetiver&lt;/a&gt;, and others. My last name is pronounced SILL-GHEE (two syllables, short &lt;code&gt;i&lt;/code&gt;, hard &lt;code&gt;g&lt;/code&gt;). I love making beautiful charts, the statistical programming language R, Jane Austen, black coffee, and red wine.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;In school, I studied physics and astronomy; I worked in academia (teaching and doing research) and ed tech before moving into data science in 2015 and discovering R. I am an author, an international speaker, and a real-world practitioner focusing on data analysis and machine learning. I have written books with my collaborators about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tidytextmining.com/&quot;&gt;text mining&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://smltar.com/&quot;&gt;supervised machine learning for text&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tmwr.org/&quot;&gt;modeling with tidy data principles&lt;/a&gt; in R.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I live in Salt Lake City, UT, with my husband, three kids, and two cats.&lt;/p&gt; 
